    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "validation: clean up failed AssumeUTXO databases",
    "user": {
      "login": "l0rinc",
      "id": 1841944,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDE5NDQ=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1841944?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/l0rinc",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/l0rinc/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "**Problem:** AssumeUTXO can leave unusable database state after failures in two lifecycle phases.\r\n\r\nAn interrupted background-chainstate cleanup can leave a nonempty `chainstate_todelete` database. The next cleanup attempt cannot rename the validated background database over that path, which prevents startup from completing.\r\n\r\n`loadtxoutset` also reduces the active chainstate caches before opening and populating `chainstate_snapshot`. If database initialization or snapshot population throws, the exception bypasses the existing cleanup path. The running node can retain both active cache budgets at 1%, and a partial snapshot database can remain without its required `base_blockhash` marker.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Remove an obsolete cleanup database before resetting the live chainstates and renaming directories. Install snapshot-activation cleanup before database initialization and reuse it for initialization and population exceptions. Snapshot-activation cleanup restores the active cache allocation, releases the snapshot database handle, and removes an unusable snapshot directory before propagating the original exception.",
